<title>USA: Lockheed Martin to settle defense dispute.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin to settle defense dispute.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp will pay $5.3 million to the U.S. federal government to settle a defense contract dispute, the Justice Department said Monday.</p>
<p>The department said the settlement resolved allegations that the Martin Marietta Corp, now part of Lockheed Martin, overcharged the Defense Department by deliberately bidding low to win a contract for a supersonic low-altitude missile target and then boosting research and development costs.</p>
</text>
